    <briefdescription>
<para>This class is used to track the last run of a set of module/function passes. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Invalidation are conservatively handled by the pass manager if a pass doesn&apos;t explicitly preserve the result. If we want to skip a pass, we should define a unique <ref refid="namespacellvm_1_1_calling_conv_1abdf8cf606905c10634e831390981b0ed" kindref="member">ID</ref> <computeroutput><ref refid="classllvm_1_1_last_run_tracking_info_1ae3d69914220ce815fe1b92211a19c8b8" kindref="member">PassID</ref></computeroutput> to identify the pass, which is usually a pointer to a static member. If a pass has parameters, they should be stored in a struct <computeroutput>OptionT</computeroutput> with a method bool isCompatibleWith(const OptionT&amp; LastOpt) const to check compatibility. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
